An Oklahoma-based project to help Iraq establish democracy is getting national and international recognition, as the group plans to meet with President Bush and send a former Iraqi scientist to the war-torn country to investigate Sad
dam Hussein's weapons program.
\par The Iraqi Democracy Project, started by the Oklahoma City-based Middle Eastern American Association, aims to get Iraqi refugee groups from throughout the country involved in rebuilding a post-Saddam Iraq. The group plans to m
eet with President Bush, U.S. State Department officials and congressional leaders in June, and also plans trips to Iraq to help the country form a democratic system.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 
\f1\fs22\lang1033\langfe1035\langnp1033\insrsid3283723\charrsid2713217 
